.\" whytime-completions(1), hand-written. cargo xtask man adds the title and
.\" replaces each ".\" @SECTION" line with that section rendered from cli.rs.
.SH NAME
whytime\-completions \- print a shell completion script for whytime
.\" @SYNOPSIS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B whytime completions
prints to standard output a script that makes
.I SHELL
complete
.BR whytime 's
subcommands and options.
.PP
The distribution packages (Debian, RPM, Alpine, Arch Linux, Nix) and the
install script already install the bash, zsh and fish scripts; this command
is for other installations and other shells.
.SH FILES
Where the system-wide scripts go, and where a user can put their own:
.TP
.B bash
.I /usr/share/bash\-completion/completions/whytime
.br
.I \(ti/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/whytime
.TP
.B zsh
.I /usr/share/zsh/site\-functions/_whytime
(Arch Linux, Fedora, Alpine;
.I /usr/share/zsh/vendor\-completions/_whytime
on Debian and Ubuntu)
.br
a file named
.I _whytime
in a directory of
.B $fpath
listed before
.B compinit
runs, for example
.I \(ti/.zfunc/_whytime
with
.B fpath=(\(ti/.zfunc $fpath)
in
.IR \(ti/.zshrc .
.TP
.B fish
.I /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/whytime.fish
.br
.I \(ti/.config/fish/completions/whytime.fish
.TP
.B elvish
Evaluate the script from
.IR \(ti/.config/elvish/rc.elv :
.B eval (whytime completions elvish | slurp)
.TP
.B powershell
Evaluate the script from the profile
.RB ( $PROFILE ):
.B whytime completions powershell | Out\-String | Invoke\-Expression
.PP
Installations under
.I /usr/local
use
.I /usr/local/share
instead of
.IR /usr/share .
A new shell picks the script up.
.\" @OPTIONS
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The script was written.
.TP
.B 1
Writing to standard output failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage, such as an unknown shell.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install the bash completions for the current user:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
dir=\(ti/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions
mkdir \-p "$dir" && whytime completions bash >"$dir/whytime"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Install the zsh completions system-wide on Arch Linux or Fedora:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
whytime completions zsh |
    sudo tee /usr/share/zsh/site\-functions/_whytime >/dev/null
.EE
.RE
.PP
Install the fish completions for the current user:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
whytime completions fish >\(ti/.config/fish/completions/whytime.fish
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR whytime (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR zsh (1),
.BR fish (1)
